icy", "reason": "ours and CatBoost fit this loss on the symmetric grower only; XGBoost has none and runs depthwise at the same depth", "theirs": "depthwise"}, {"arm": "xgboost-cpu", "ours": null, "param": "min_child_weight", "reason": "ours takes min_child_hessian on Depthwise and Lossguide only; on the symmetric grower it is unset (no hessian floor, as CatBoost; XGBoost 0)", "theirs": 0.0}, {"arm": "xgboost-cpu", "ours": null, "param": "min_split_gain", "reason": "ours takes min_split_gain on Depthwise and Lossguide only; on the symmetric grower it is unset (CatBoost has none; XGBoost gamma 0, LightGBM 0)", "theirs": 0.0}, {"arm": "xgboost-cpu", "ours": null, "param": "subsample", "reason": "no row sampling on any arm: ours and CatBoost bootstrap_type 'No' (neither accepts subsample beside it, so it stays unset), XGBoost and LightGBM subsample 1.0", "theirs": 1.0}, {"arm": "lightgbm-cpu", "ours": "Plain", "param": "boosting_type", "reason": "different vocabularies: ours and CatBoost 'Plain' (not Ordered), LightGBM 'gbdt'; both plain gradient boosting", "theirs": "gbdt"}, {"arm": "lightgbm-cpu", "ours": null, "param": "min_child_weight", "reason": "LightGBM 4.7.0 aborts a boosted tree at min_child_weight 0 (best_split_info.left_count > 0) and keeps 1e-3; ours has no hessian floor", "theirs": 0.001}, {"arm": "lightgbm-cpu", "ours": 1, "param": "min_samples_leaf", "reason": "LightGBM keeps min_child_samples 20 (it aborts at the other arms' value); ours and CatBoost min_data_in_leaf 1", "theirs": 20}, {"arm": "lightgbm-cpu", "ours": null, "param": "min_split_gain", "reason": "ours takes min_split_gain on Depthwise and Lossguide only; on the symmetric grower it is unset (CatBoost has none; XGBoost gamma 0, LightGBM 0)", "theirs": 0.0}, {"arm": "lightgbm-cpu", "ours": null, "param": "subsample", "reason": "no row sampling on any arm: ours and CatBoost bootstrap_type 'No' (neither accepts subsample beside it, so it stays unset), XGBoost and LightGBM subsample 1.0", "their